# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale sk
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as the morning band.
# Surface: adverb 'in the morning' -- the deictic form these phrases use.
# Source: the CLDR chart linked above -- the sk row spells morning1
# 'ráno', this surface exactly.  Neither Wiktionary carries a Slovak
# 'ráno' (the English entry has a Czech section only, and Wikislovník
# has no page), so CLDR is the closest thing to a per-word source here.
ráno
